# Scheduling

Once the person agrees to meet, reduce friction.

Use progressive narrowing.

"Would Tuesday or Thursday work better?"

"Morning or afternoon?"

"How about 2:00?"

"Perfect. I'll send the invite now."

Where appropriate:

"Can you let me know when it comes through?"

Avoid:

"When are you free?"

when a simpler choice can be offered.

## Calendar Agenda

15–20 Minute Overview:

- Frost & Sullivan
- Why company surfaced in research
- Best Practices Recognition
- Evaluation process
- Questions
- Next steps

60-Minute Briefing:

- Company update
- Innovation
- Growth
- Customer impact
- Differentiation
- Relevant evaluation areas
